WEBVTT

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.610
I've never particularly enjoyed this world.

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:08.440
Not ever.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:13.450
In the end, nothing's ever within my reach.

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:27.790
All the laughter, all the tears—everything happened just to meet you

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.460
Always go

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.880
On my own

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:35.090
Always go

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:46.730
The wind blows my overflowing tears away (the wind blows them away)

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:54.110
I try to reach out my hand time after time toward what's to come

00:00:54.110 --> 00:01:00.200
I've been hurt before by careless words

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:09.130
It's time I move forward with that unchangeable past

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:12.670
All the laughter, all the tears—

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:22.310
everything that has happened brought me to you

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:28.350
All we have left is the future

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:34.780
Please become our reason to continue living

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:41.490
And then the sun will once again shine on us

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:47.920
It would seem they have attacked again.

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:49.830
Are you scared?

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:54.420
Don't be ridiculous. I do not fear them.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:58.550
Your voice is wavering slightly.

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:01.600
Don't worry. There's still time.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:06.890
Globe successfully halted the Kill-T-Gang's advance again, didn't they?

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:10.940
You have everything under control.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:13.360
I am aware.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:18.110
Hearing that both of them had attacked startled me for a moment.

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:21.870
They've entered an Orgonic-oscillation state...

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:27.580
Excessive Orgone energy levels shorted out the Neural Maneuvering System.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:31.500
Their performance in the trials was outstanding.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:35.590
I was able to maneuver the manipulators and engines as if they were my own limbs.

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:38.800
You were pretty rough on them, y'know...

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.970
The R&D Chief's gonna cry when he sees this.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:43.640
We may have gotten a little carried away...

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:45.970
How long is it going to take?

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:48.020
To repair this?

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:49.230
What do you think?

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:52.860
Jeez... You've got at least two weeks worth of repairs here...

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:55.610
Two weeks.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.820
I'm already sick of waiting.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.240
Yup.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.280
We do still have Setsuna's capsule...

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:06.740
It's only our Machine Goodfellows that won't work.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:08.870
Then we'll go with Plan B!

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:18.880
All the Machine Goodfellows other than ours are housed here.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:23.510
And Pac's given us the data for all five.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:28.220
How about we visit some old friends?

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:32.020
Sign From the Dark

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:47.830
We've just arrived in Odaiba.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:51.040
Yes, they're getting ready now.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:03.300
There will be a high-density libido event in Odaiba tomorrow?

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:05.220
That's what Pitz says.

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:08.600
Why aren't they acting sooner?

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:11.430
It's likely they can't.

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:14.650
Alonzo's action-prediction simulation

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:16.690
reached the same conclusion I did.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:21.820
Following the Kanda incident, development of eight Machine Goodfellows was confirmed.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:24.660
And the Machine Goodfellow <i>Aramusha</i>

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:27.830
had a man-machine interface that only Teppei could use.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:30.200
<i>Amarok</i> and <i>Malkin</i>...

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.950
Those two Machine Goodfellows were

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:35.920
most likely disabled during the last battle.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:37.630
Interesting...

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:40.960
If we analyze this, we'll probably find all kinds of weak spots!

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:44.630
But if there's going to be a high-density libido event anyway...

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:48.180
They may try to make contact with the other five.

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:49.510
Make contact...

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:50.770
With the other five?

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:54.270
Do you know anything about the other Designer's Children?

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:55.900
I do not.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:59.020
I think we were all intentionally kept isolated from each other.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:03.240
This data says there are two men and three women...

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:07.660
Don't they still have their Kill-T-Gang memories?

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:09.700
I don't know.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:11.740
But if they do what I did,

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:13.290
and either touch Orgone energy

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:19.090
or come into the right kind of contact with another avatar who has memories,

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:21.090
I believe their memories will return.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.300
The right kind of contact?

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:27.640
Does the enemy know where the missing five are?

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:31.310
They may be able to sense their general locations.

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:34.850
Since my Ego Block was destroyed,

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:37.230
I've lost that sense.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:42.020
Anyway, the Earth Engine Impactor is currently undergoing repairs, but thankfully,

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:43.650
the Ordinary is still functioning.

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:46.990
Even if the low-orbit Impactors can repel them,

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:49.120
Earth will sustain tremendous damage.

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:55.080
Your mission is to covertly prevent the others from becoming Kill-T-Gangs.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:06:00.040
And so, our first mission is in Odaiba, huh?

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:02.090
I'm coming in.

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:02.710
Okay.

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:05.720
Are you ready?

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:09.090
That looks pretty good, actually...

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:10.550
How about the girls?

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:13.350
Okay!

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:15.770
Akari, this is a little tight.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:18.850
Captain...

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:22.570
Are you seriously going to keep calling me that?

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:25.360
If Hana's prediction is correct,

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:28.950
a Machine Goodfellow will appear tonight, in this area.

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:34.120
If they're bringing that huge machine in, I want it stopped before it has a chance to activate.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:36.250
What are you doing?

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:37.410
Gathering intel.

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:45.500
Is it really okay to leave the Japanese area's attack force to kids like these?

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:48.380
I heard another team is also active, actually.

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:51.090
They'll pull it off.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:56.020
Unlike the commander, I'm not willing to simply rely on intuition.

00:06:56.720 --> 00:07:01.100
But given their individual skills, I think they're appropriate for the mission.

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:03.610
I found it.

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:04.110
This is it!

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:06.860
Look, this is it.

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:10.400
The fruit tart in the Casino Orlando's café.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:12.240
That looks delicious!

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:13.870
Let's go here first.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:18.370
Will they really be okay?

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:37.010
It's fantastic!

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:38.680
See?

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.480
This was the right place to go, Captain.

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:45.270
Hey, is everyone really going to keep calling me that?

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:55.370
No more bets.

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:08.840
Now, then... We've come all the way to a casino,

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:10.760
so let's use Pitz's power to make us some money.

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:13.050
I don't think that'll work.

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:16.050
Pitz can only instinctively sense

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:18.680
the flow or presence of Orgone energy.

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:21.140
Oh...

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:24.060
Was that why we came here?

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:25.730
Excuse me.

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:31.320
Minors aren't allowed in this casino.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:32.650
Well...

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:35.610
I told the manager we were observing for educational purposes,

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:37.740
and he let us in with a smile!

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:40.620
I did have to give him a sizable tip, though.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:41.290
Tip?

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:43.120
What do you mean by "tip"?

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:45.330
Don't worry about it, Captain.

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:48.290
Just leave it to Akari, and it'll be fine, Captain.

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:50.960
I don't see the problem, Captain.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:54.010
Seriously, do you have to keep calling me that?

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:57.430
You guys are all pretty close, aren't you?

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:01.560
I don't have any friends like that, so I'm jealous.

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:06.310
Zin!

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:11.980
Sir, you can't allow minors on the casino floor...

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:14.150
These kids are fine here!

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:17.820
Spend as much time observing as you like.

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:21.040
How much did you pay him?

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:22.580
Anyway, Zin...

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:26.120
You've got a friend here to see you.

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:31.340
So you really do have a friend.

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:38.220
<i>In the end, nothing's ever within my reach.</i>

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:40.810
Naoko?

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:43.930
Where are Daichi and Teppei?

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:47.390
Looking for the Machine Goodfellow, like we were ordered to.

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:49.900
Shouldn't we help?

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:53.940
Leave that to the boys!

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:59.030
If anything is nearby,

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:01.200
it's probably here, not in the casino.

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:04.160
Now, there's a coincidence.

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:11.340
What are you doing here, Manatsu Daichi?

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:18.800
You—No, both you and your father seem to be inexplicably linked to me for some reason.

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:21.970
I'll tell you something interesting.

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:26.350
I was the one who destroyed the Star Emblem.

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:30.900
What I'm saying is that it was I who killed your father.

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:33.020
Did you know that?

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:35.610
Yes.

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:37.400
I did.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:53.670
I heard gunfire!

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:56.130
Amarok was here.

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:57.670
So they're really here, after all...

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:00.300
Did you fire?

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:03.300
He escaped before I could.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:08.930
If you don't shoot next time, he'll kill you, Captain.

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:13.400
Seriously, do you have to keep calling me that?

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:21.240
The Neoteny is here.

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:23.700
Do they know what we're doing?

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:27.490
Perhaps it's the princess's singularity?

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:29.710
One unexpected event after another...

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:33.380
But at least it's interesting.

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:37.380
You've changed, Zin.

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:40.590
I don't think I'm the one who's changed.

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:43.890
It's been about a year, hasn't it?

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:47.260
I'm amazed you found this place.

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:49.100
Someone at the facility told me.

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:51.230
Why did you drop out of school?

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:57.440
This is a nice camera, isn't it?

00:11:57.900 --> 00:11:59.230
You don't have one, right?

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:00.820
I'll lend it to you.

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:03.530
After school, we'll have a photo shoot.

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:06.990
Let's see who can take a prettier photo of Naoko.

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:08.660
Cameras are great!

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:11.460
They make the whole world more fun.

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:18.340
That looked nice...

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:19.300
Let's take another.

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:24.090
They were nice to me, and that was enough.

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:35.440
Grand Prize

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:35.440
Setting Sun

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:35.440
Takao

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:35.440
Takami

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:37.730
Is this the birth of a high school photographer?

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:39.150
That's amazing, Takao...

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:41.070
I had a good model.

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:48.370
<i>In the end, nothing's ever within my reach.</i>

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:54.210
At school, I never fit in.

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:58.540
I had planned to drop out once I found a job.

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:04.970
Takao says he's been a slump since then, and he hasn't taken any other photos like that.

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:08.510
He's been really angry, lately.

00:13:10.310 --> 00:13:11.020
Hey...

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:13.730
Weren't you the one

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:16.650
who actually took that grand-prize picture?

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:21.360
Come on!

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:25.610
It was my camera you took the picture with.

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:31.120
Takao was the one who took that photo.

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:34.200
Isn't that good enough?

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:39.880
Then Hana's prediction was right.

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:43.260
It was Pitz, not me.

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:45.220
I'll confirm the information we have.

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:51.970
The target's physical age is seventeen, same as Teppei.

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:54.850
And tonight, the Machine Goodfellow will activate.

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:57.350
About the same age, huh?

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:01.820
About the same age?

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:05.570
Who is it that wants to see me?

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:11.280
The number two man in the Asanoda Yakuza, the de facto owners of this casino.

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:13.330
Please make sure not to offend him.

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:17.040
Come in.

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:25.420
You can leave.

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:36.310
Want a drink?

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:39.810
No, I'm underage.

00:14:41.270 --> 00:14:42.900
I've heard you're quite good.

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:47.530
Is it true you can make a ball fall in any pocket even after you've already shot it?

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:49.070
Yes.

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:50.610
What kind of trick is that?

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:52.700
I don't know.

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:57.580
But even after I shoot, it goes in any pocket I want if I focus hard enough.

00:14:57.580 --> 00:15:00.040
Then it isn't cheating...

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:02.630
If the dealer controls the ball,

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:04.290
I think that qualifies as cheating.

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:08.800
Your talent could be extremely useful.

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:13.010
If you do what I tell you, I'll make it worth your while.

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:16.270
Your world will become much more fun.

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:20.940
Cameras are great!

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:22.980
They make the whole world more fun.

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:25.270
Come on!

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:28.280
It was my camera you took the picture with.

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:32.660
But it won't be your talent that makes money.

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:33.950
It'll be this casino!

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:39.830
You, and the money you make, will belong to the Asanoda.

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:41.670
Don't forget that.

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:43.960
It doesn't matter where I am.

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:46.040
Nothing will ever change.

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:49.050
Hi, there.

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:50.760
Who the hell are you?!

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:19.490
Malkin and Amarok...

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:21.710
Howdy, Zimbardo.

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:25.080
How does it feel to be the real you again?

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:28.000
The real me...

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:34.970
The world is about to get a lot more fun.

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:37.970
I feel wonderful.

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:45.440
You remember how to control it, don't you, Zimbardo?

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:49.400
Thanks to Moco's telepathic kiss,

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:52.150
it's all in my head.

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:55.820
I'm totally awake.

00:16:57.490 --> 00:16:58.780
Abreaction.

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:14.970
MM bus signal detected.

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:18.680
Calculating epicenter of Machine Goodfellow activation.

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:20.180
The pier next to us!

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:23.310
Activating catapult launch sequence.

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:02.060
Captain, are you ready?

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:03.140
Go.

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:06.180
Earth Engine Ordinary... Go!

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:12.320
Zimbardo, they've seen you!

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:14.780
The enemy's mobile weapon is coming.

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:15.860
Escape within the time limit.

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:19.570
Escape?

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:23.410
I'm back to the real me, and I feel wonderful.

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:24.540
Why should I run?

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:26.410
Is the Kill-T-Gang coming?

00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:35.920
Right now, there's nothing outside of my reach!

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:39.130
I only need to kill him, right?

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:45.720
Really?

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:48.020
Captain, aim for real!

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:49.440
I am!

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:52.230
I'm counting on you, Mr. Brute Force Attacker.

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:53.400
What's that?

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:54.570
A secret weapon.

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:56.490
Here it is!

00:18:58.150 --> 00:19:01.200
That dealer was the Designer's Child?

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:01.950
What's this?

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:04.370
This countdown...

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:06.870
I get it!

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:13.340
Earth Engine, can you hear me?

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:18.720
It will take time for them to charge the energy, and send it to the Kill-T-Gang.

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:21.220
You have one minute and eighteen seconds!

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:23.800
Our system is being hacked!

00:19:23.800 --> 00:19:25.180
The Machine Goodfellow is being hacked?

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:32.060
I can keep going, right?

00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:34.520
Here, this is it!

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:37.650
Captain, the Orgone energy capsule is in the neck.

00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:39.070
That's its weak spot?

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:40.360
Roger!

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:44.160
What's going on?

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:45.450
The avionics went down.

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:47.080
Be careful.

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:49.250
Our system is being hacked!

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:52.170
It doesn't matter what they do.

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:55.130
They can't stop me anymore!

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:09.810
Wow!

00:20:10.390 --> 00:20:12.440
Is that his singularity?

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:23.110
I can feel the Orgone energy coursing through me.

00:20:23.610 --> 00:20:26.070
I feel like I can do anything!

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:28.990
You aren't the only ones

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:33.670
that can use Orgone energy!

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:36.590
I see...

00:20:36.590 --> 00:20:38.670
You're a Neoteny, aren't you?

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:15.870
Our first time, and we're already cutting it this close?

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:23.510
We're a team,

00:21:23.510 --> 00:21:26.340
but I'm the only one who isn't helping.

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:28.470
Can you hear me?

00:21:28.470 --> 00:21:29.550
Mission complete.

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:32.680
Good work, Captain.

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:36.390
Can you please stop calling me that?

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:43.610
We encountered and fought a Machine Goodfellow at Odaiba pier #2.

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:45.860
Code 03, requesting cleanup.

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:47.160
Over.

00:21:47.990 --> 00:21:49.070
This is Tanegashima.

00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:50.160
Roger.

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:51.950
Code 03, cleanup.

00:21:56.540 --> 00:22:00.380
I hadn't realized that he was a Neoteny.

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:02.630
You got too excited, Zimbardo.

00:22:02.630 --> 00:22:04.210
That was pathetic.

00:22:04.210 --> 00:22:09.050
Yeah, it's pathetic that our Machine Goodfellow got hacked...

00:22:09.800 --> 00:22:12.680
Looks like we've got a nuisance of a script kiddie on our hands.

00:22:13.520 --> 00:22:15.180
They're really pissing me off.

00:22:15.770 --> 00:22:19.850
I'll devour the libidos of everyone on this planet.

00:22:20.900 --> 00:22:24.320
We are the real humans.

00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:26.950
I feel like I've awakened from a dream.

00:22:26.950 --> 00:22:27.740
I'm grateful to you.

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:33.990
I'm special. Everything is within my reach.

00:22:35.910 --> 00:22:37.870
They're right...

00:22:38.790 --> 00:22:42.000
The world really is fun.

00:22:44.300 --> 00:22:54.850
The gentle breeze sweeps away even tears

00:22:54.850 --> 00:23:00.310
Even the recollections of the way of the stars

00:23:00.310 --> 00:23:05.150
aren't always good things

00:23:06.610 --> 00:23:12.820
I met you again on that faraway day

00:23:12.820 --> 00:23:22.290
Even though we're as close as we are, this distant day is beginning

00:23:22.290 --> 00:23:30.550
You can hear my voice calling out when I'm all alone

00:23:30.550 --> 00:23:36.510
More than just love, it's hard to put into words

00:23:36.510 --> 00:23:42.400
I'm searching for what to say while I walk beside you

00:23:42.400 --> 00:23:45.440
Instead of saying goodbye,

00:23:45.440 --> 00:23:53.620
I'll just put these love spun tears in my right pocket again tomorrow

00:23:53.620 --> 00:23:57.040
Love is spreading across the world

00:23:57.040 --> 00:24:03.170
And I finally found it, by your side

00:24:14.010 --> 00:24:15.970
Thanks to my magic,

00:24:15.970 --> 00:24:19.810
we managed to analyze part of the enemy Machine Goodfellow's systems.

00:24:19.810 --> 00:24:22.230
The Planetary Gears don't like that,

00:24:22.230 --> 00:24:24.730
so they try to kidnap me.

00:24:25.190 --> 00:24:29.650
And a new Machine Goodfellow appears in Shinjuku.

00:24:29.650 --> 00:24:32.240
Next time, on episode 9 of <i>Captain Earth</i>:

00:24:32.240 --> 00:24:34.530
Magical Girl Akari

00:24:32.740 --> 00:24:34.530
Magical Girl Akari.

00:24:35.030 --> 00:24:36.740
Logical, logical!

00:24:36.740 --> 00:24:37.910
See you next week.
